  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Consider a frame that is made up of two thin massless rods <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>C</mi></math> as shown in the figure. A vertical force <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>P</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></math>&nbsp;of magnitude <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math> is applied at point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> of the frame.</p><p><img src=\"assets\\qt0112_e5482dc9c244.png\" style=\"width: 141px; height: 266px;\" /></p><p>Suppose the force is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>P</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></math>&nbsp;resolved parallel to the arms <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>C</mi></math> of the frame. The magnitude of the resolved component along the arm <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>C</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mi>N</mi></math>. The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>, to the nearest integer, is ________.</p><p>[Given :&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>35</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>573</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>cos</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>35</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>819</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>110</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>939</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>cos</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>110</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>342</mn></math>]</p>"
  },
